  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/75BFBD">Definition <span data-tag="75BFBD">5.2.8.1</span>.</a>orthogonalorthogonal!leftorthogonal!rightleft orthogonalright orthogonal Let $f: A \rightarrow B$ and $g: X \rightarrow Y$ be morphisms in an $\infty $-category $\calC $. We will say that $f$ is <em>left orthogonal</em> to $g$, or that $g$ is <em>right orthogonal to $f$</em>, if the following condition is satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(\ast )$"><p>
For every commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { A \ar [r] \ar [d]^{f} &  X \ar [d]^{g} \\ B \ar [r] &  Y } \]
</div>
<p>
 in $\calC $, the mapping space $\bHom _{\calC _{A/ \,  /Y}}(B,X )$ is contractible. (Here we abuse notation by identifying $B$ and $X$ with the corresponding objects of $\calC _{A/\, /Y}$.) 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p> In this case, we will write $f \perp g$.fperpg@$f \perp g$ </p>
